---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import TimeLineElement from "../components/cv/TimeLine.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Curriculum Vitae" sideBarActiveItemID="cv">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Profile</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 text-justify">
    Master's student in Computer Science (Cloud Computing & Infrastructure) with hands-on
    experience in backend development, REST APIs, Docker, and CI/CD. Fluent in English (C1) and
    comfortable in international, agile environments. Seeking a software engineering / DevOps &
    automation internship.
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Education</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container grid gap-4 mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Master 2 in Computer Science (MoSIG) — Cloud Computing & Infrastructure"
      subtitle="Sep 2026 – Present at Grenoble INP - Ensimag / Université Grenoble Alpes, Grenoble, France"
    >
      Relevant courses: Cloud Computing, Large-Scale Data Management, Computer Security, Model
      Checking & Formal Verification, Performance Evaluation, Advanced Software Engineering.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Engineering Degree in Systems and Computer Science (Bac+5)"
      subtitle="2020 – 2025 at Universidad del Norte, Barranquilla, Colombia"
    >
      Relevant courses: Software Design & Architecture, Operating Systems, Computer Networks,
      Databases, Algorithms & Complexity, Compilers.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Experience</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="R&D Intern in Software Engineering & Research (SusInnoS Project)"
      subtitle="Feb 2026 – Sep 2026 at Laboratoire G-SCOP (CNRS / UGA), Grenoble, France"
    >
      Designed a semantic search engine (NLP) combining Sentence-BERT, FAISS, and Cross-Encoder to
      automatically map industrial nomenclatures (BOM) to the Ecoinvent database.<br />
      Developed the Life Cycle Assessment (LCA) calculation pipeline via Brightway and a REST API
      backend using Python, Django, PostgreSQL, SQLite, and Docker, with CI/CD automation.<br />
      Performed model benchmarks (Hugging Face), wrote automated tests (Pytest), and technical
      specifications (Markdown, JSON schemas).
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Mentorship Lead — ACM Student Chapter"
      subtitle="Feb 2024 – Aug 2025 at Universidad del Norte, Barranquilla, Colombia"
    >
      Led the technical mentorship program, coordinated development workshops, and provided
      academic support to computer science students.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Programming Instructor & Teaching Assistant"
      subtitle="Feb 2022 – May 2025 at Universidad del Norte, Barranquilla, Colombia"
    >
      Ran hands-on workshops in Python and Java (OOP, algorithms) and provided teaching assistance
      for the Introduction to Computer Science course (exercise design, code review).
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Projects & Research</div>
  </div>

  <div class="time-line-container mb-10">
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Transcription & Contextualization System (Capstone)"
      subtitle="Python, Vosk, ChromaDB, JavaScript · 2025"
    >
      Open-source web application converting audio recordings into Markdown study guides,
      integrating a fine-tuned Vosk ASR model with contextual vector search via ChromaDB.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Rubik's Race — Heuristic Solving"
      subtitle="Python, A* Algorithm, Manhattan Distance · 2025"
    >
      Web application solving Rubik's Race via the A* algorithm with a custom heuristic combining
      Manhattan distance and a bonus term for completed rows.
    </TimeLineElement>
    <TimeLineElement
      title="Huesitos — Medical Image Analysis & AI"
      subtitle="Python, TensorFlow, Scikit-learn, OpenCV, Gradio · 2024"
    >
      CNN-based fracture detection system on X-rays with a confidence threshold below 25%, creation
      of an annotated dataset (600+ images), and comparison of feature extraction methods against
      deep learning.
    </TimeLineElement>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-5">
    <div class="text-3xl w-full font-bold">Skills</div>
  </div>

  <div class="mb-10 space-y-2">
    <p><span class="font-semibold">Programming Languages:</span> Python, SQL, JavaScript, Java, C</p>
    <p><span class="font-semibold">Cloud, DevOps & Tools:</span> Docker, Git, GitHub Actions, Linux (Bash), Pytest, Azure, Kubernetes (notions), CI/CD, Postman</p>
    <p><span class="font-semibold">Backend & Databases:</span> Django, Node.js, REST APIs, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, SQLite, MySQL, ChromaDB (Vector DB)</p>
    <p><span class="font-semibold">AI & Scientific Computing:</span> OpenAI, Gemini, Hugging Face, Sentence-BERT, FAISS, Brightway (LCA), TensorFlow, Scikit-learn</p>
    <p><span class="font-semibold">Languages:</span> English (Fluent — C1), Spanish (Native), French (Intermediate — B1 in progress)</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
